# fixedbugs, defect 022, panel 122, 2026-09-09.
#
# SYMPTOM: silent at `heroes check`, and `--sanitize` reports
# `AddressSanitizer: heap-use-after-free`, READ of size 7. Both compiling
# seats at panel 122 built this shape independently, from opposite ends.
#
# CAUSE: the lend stands in an ARGUMENT position, which the position rule
# blesses, and what leaves the frame is the helper's RESULT. No rule about
# where a `.cstr()` may stand can see it, which is why the sitting's first
# recommendation — the coordinator's — had this hole and shipped nothing.
#
# FIX: panel 122 R3, the signature rule, which closes the whole route at the
# declaration instead of chasing the flow. Both functions here are refused,
# and that is the point: each one answers `cstr` outside a group.

extern "string.h"
    function strlen(s: cstr) -> u64

function pass(c: cstr) -> cstr  #~ cstr_out_of_heroes
    return c

function outer(n: i64) -> cstr  #~ cstr_out_of_heroes
    return pass(c: ("heap-" + n.to_str()).cstr())

function main()
    print(strlen(s: outer(n: 7)).to_str())
